{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetM3m1dzbTuy4S1sFChP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me summarize the findings for the analysis phase.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt (line 11-16) - currently has orderId, customerId, amount, currency; needs status field\n- OrderController.kt (line 15-46) - has create and get endpoints; needs cancel endpoint\n- OrderRepository.kt (line 11-27) - simple in-memory store with save, findById, findAll, existsById, clear\n- Shipment.kt (line 9-27) - has shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status (ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt (line 21-56) - create endpoint doesn't check order status\n- ShipmentRepository.kt (line 11-27) - like OrderRepository, needs method to find all shipments for an order\n- ApiExceptions.kt (line 11-24) - defines ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ApiError.kt (line 31-37) - ErrorCode enum with ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt (line 14-28) - handles ApiException and converts to ApiError response\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses rather than building error responses\n- Error codes are centralized in the ErrorCode enum\n- Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for in-memory storage\n- Tests use MockMvc and assert on both status and response body (including error.code)\n- Tests after state-changing calls verify the state through a separate GET request\n- New orders/shipments are created with @PostMapping returning 201 CREATED\n- Not found errors use ResourceNotFoundException with ErrorCode\n- Conflict errors use ConflictException with ErrorCode\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - Add `status: OrderStatus` field and `OrderStatus` enum (required for state management)\n2. `OrderController.kt` - Add POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (required by ticket)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Add method to find shipments by orderId (required to cancel all CREATED shipments and check for CONFIRMED)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add order status check in create endpoint (required to prevent shipment creation on CANCELLED orders)\n5. `ApiError.kt` - Add error code for ORDER_CANCELLED (required for error response consistency)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for cancel endpoint behavior (required for acceptance criteria)\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order (required for requirement)\n\n**Risks:**\n- The cancel operation needs to be atomic: either all shipments are cancelled and order is moved to CANCELLED, or nothing changes. The current in-memory architecture doesn't have transactional support, but since operations are synchronous and single-threaded, we can implement this by checking first before any changes.\n- Adding a status field to Order changes its shape; existing tests that create orders without status will need updating or the Order constructor needs a default value.\n- ShipmentController needs access to OrderRepository to check order status - this couples the modules but is necessary for the requirement.\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified that would change the correct behavior. The requirement is clear about:\n- Idempotent cancel (already CANCELLED = success, change nothing)\n- All-or-nothing semantics (CONFIRMED shipment blocks ALL changes)\n- 409 for cancelled orders (no 404)\n- 404 for non-existent orders\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field with enum defining `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` states. Default newly created orders to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - If already CANCELLED, returns 200 OK with the order (idempotent)\n   - If ACTIVE and any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException (409) with no changes\n   - If ACTIVE, cancels all CREATED shipments, moves order to CANCELLED, saves and returns the order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - In the create endpoint, after checking shipmentId uniqueness, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to ErrorCode enum for consistency\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order: verify it transitions to CANCELLED and shipments are updated\n   - Cancel an already CANCELLED order: verify it succeeds and changes nothing\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment: verify 409 and no changes\n   - Cancel non-existent order: verify 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order: verify 409\n\n**Alternative approach rejected:**\n- Create a separate OrderService class: The existing codebase has no service layer and keeps business logic in controllers for simplicity. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring outside the scope. Keeping logic in the controller maintains consistency.\n- Use transactions for atomicity: Not applicable to in-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage. Instead, we verify constraints first, then apply all changes in sequence.\n- Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code only for shipment creation: The requirement says error responses should be consistent with the rest of the API, and ORDER_CANCELLED is conceptually part of the error catalog. But we could use CONFLICT without a specific code. Actually, looking at the existing patterns, ConflictException uses ErrorCode enums. We should add ORDER_CANCELLED for consistency and future clarity.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Success: Cancel ACTIVE order*\n- POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- OrderController.cancel() calls repository.findById(orderId)\n- If not found: throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) → 404\n- If found and CANCELLED: skip to return\n- If found and ACTIVE:\n  - Get all shipments by orderId from ShipmentRepository\n  - Check if any have status CONFIRMED\n  - If yes: throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS) → 409, no changes\n  - If no: \n    - Cancel all CREATED shipments (set status to CANCELLED)\n    - Set order status to CANCELLED\n    - Save order and all modified shipments\n    - Return updated order with 200 OK\n\n*Error: Duplicate cancel (idempotent)*\n- Same as above, but order already CANCELLED\n- Skip shipment cancellation logic, return order as-is\n\n*Error: Order has CONFIRMED shipment*\n- POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- Check shipment statuses\n- Throw ConflictException → 409, no changes to order or shipments\n\n*Error: Non-existent order*\n- POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- repository.findById() returns null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException → 404\n\n*Error: Create shipment on CANCELLED order*\n- POST /shipments with orderId pointing to CANCELLED order\n- ShipmentController.create() calls orderRepository.findById(request.orderId)\n- If order exists and status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) → 409\n- If order doesn't exist: create shipment (current behavior preserved)\n- If order exists and status is ACTIVE: create shipment\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- `test_cancel_active_order`: Create order, verify ACTIVE, cancel, verify 200 + CANCELLED, GET to verify persistence\n- `test_cancel_idempotent`: Cancel once, cancel again, verify both return 200 + CANCELLED + same response body\n- `test_cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment`: Create order, create shipment, confirm it, try cancel, verify 409 + order still ACTIVE + shipment still CONFIRMED\n- `test_cancel_cancels_created_shipments`: Create order, create 2 shipments, cancel order, verify both shipments CANCELLED\n- `test_cancel_non_existent_order`: Try cancel non-existent, verify 404 with error.code\n- `test_cancel_unchanged_after_rejection`: Verify GET after 409 shows no change\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- `test_create_shipment_on_cancelled_order`: Create order, cancel it, try create shipment, verify 409 with error.code + shipment not created\n\nOrderControllerTest modifications:\n- Existing `creates_an_order_and_returns_201` should verify order.status == ACTIVE\n- Existing `reads_back_created_order` should verify order.status == ACTIVE\n\nThe first line of code comes after this phase's marker, never before it.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_read_input_tokens":23490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1496},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1ccff5e-c312-43c5-ad0c-d00f80c30574","uuid":"e99cf56d-fe42-4551-8dba-da0c6bab91ac","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:34:35.528Z","request_id":"req_011CetM3kMh9gtk17yoqBCq4"}
