elled_order` - verifies 409 for shipment creation\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** - Only Kotlin/Spring Boot libraries already in pom.xml\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified Order.kt, OrderController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ShipmentController.kt, and ApiError.kt\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n*Order.kt* - Added `status: OrderStatus` field with default ACTIVE and OrderStatus enum. NECESSARY - Orders must track their state.\n\n*OrderController.kt* - Added cancel endpoint with logic to check for CONFIRMED shipments, cancel CREATED ones, and transition order to CANCELLED. Injected ShipmentRepository. NECESSARY - This is the ticket's core requirement.\n\n*ShipmentRepository.kt* - Added `findByOrderId()` method. NECESSARY - OrderController needs to query shipments by order.\n\n*ShipmentController.kt* - Added order status check in create endpoint to reject CANCELLED orders with 409. Injected OrderRepository. NECESSARY - Requirement states shipment creation for CANCELLED orders must be rejected.\n\n*ApiError.kt* - Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS error codes. NECESSARY - Error codes must be defined in the enum to be used.\n\n*OrderControllerTest.kt* - Added 6 new tests covering cancel scenarios and updated 2 existing tests to verify ACTIVE status on creation. NECESSARY - Comprehensive test coverage for new cancel feature.\n\n*ShipmentControllerTest.kt* - Added 1 new test for cancelled order rejection and cleared shipmentRepository in @BeforeEach. NECESSARY - Test coverage for the new requirement about cancelled orders.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All ticket requirements have been implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Customers may cancel an order until a carrier has accepted a shipment for it; cancellation is idempotent, atomically transitions the order and its CREATED shipments, rejects if any shipment is CONFIRMED, and prevents future shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added status field (OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE, CANCELLED) to track order lifecycle\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint implementing all cancel logic and shipment transitions\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() query method required by cancel logic\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added order status validation to reject shipment creation on CANCELLED orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 tests (cancel, idempotent cancel, confirmed shipment blocking, CREATED shipment cancellation, 404 case) and updated 2 existing tests to verify ACTIVE status\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for cancelled order rejection; fixed setup to clear both repositories\n\nTests:\n- `creates_an_order_and_returns_201`: Verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n- `reads_back_created_order`: Verifies GET returns ACTIVE status\n- `cancel_moves_an_active_order_to_cancelled_status`: Verifies POST /orders/{id}/cancel transitions order to CANCELLED and persists\n- `cancel_is_idempotent`: Verifies repeated cancel succeeds without changes\n- `cancel_returns_404_for_non_existent_order`: Verifies 404 for unknown order with error.code\n- `cancel_cancels_all_created_shipments`: Verifies all CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED\n- `cancel_is_rejected_when_shipment_is_confirmed`: Verifies 409 with error.code and no changes when CONFIRMED shipment exists\n- `rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order`: Verifies 409 with error.code when creating shipment for CANCELLED order\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` → BUILD SUCCESS, 19 tests passed, 0 failures\n\nNot done: Nothing - all acceptance criteria met, all tests pass, all cases covered."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3319,"cache_read_input_tokens":38394,"cache_creation":{"epheme